# The fetch role's name answer: an `internal` network has no route, so the role container cannot ask a
# resolver of its own. `resolv.conf` is this container's own -- the daemon's, on the network that does
# have a route -- so the upstream stays whatever the host already uses rather than a named third party.
. {
    errors
    forward . /etc/resolv.conf
    cache 30
}
